 in 90 minutes? What Nitin Gadkari said]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/delhi-to-haridwar-in-90-minutes-what-nitin-gadkari-said/articleshow/135254677.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135254677.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Union Road Transport and Highways Minister Nitin Gadkari announced a new road project connecting Delhi to Haridwar. This project aims to significantly reduce the travel time between the two cities to approximately 90 minutes. Improved road infrastructure will enhance access to pilgrimage sites and boost tourism. The Delhi-Mumbai Expressway will also connect rural areas to major business centers for economic growth.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/delhi-to-haridwar-in-90-minutes-what-nitin-gadkari-said/articleshow/135254677.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/delhi-to-haridwar-in-90-minutes-what-nitin-gadkari-said/articleshow/135254677.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-28T12:04:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135255141,imgsize-117451.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Prayagraj’s cultural, literary legacy celebrated at JNU festival]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/prayagrajs-cultural-literary-legacy-celebrated-at-jnu-festival/articleshow/135254352.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135254352.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Over 450 people gathered to celebrate Prayagraj's cultural and intellectual heritage at Jawaharlal Nehru University. The event featured discussions focused on the city’s literary contributions and historical significance. Musical and dance performances highlighted the area's cultural traditions and engaged different generations. Notable speakers included cabinet minister Nand Gopal Gupta and former minister Siddharth Nath Singh. This initiative promoted awareness of Prayagraj's enduring influence on contemporary thought and traditions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/prayagrajs-cultural-literary-legacy-celebrated-at-jnu-festival/articleshow/135254352.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/prayagrajs-cultural-literary-legacy-celebrated-at-jnu-festival/articleshow/135254352.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-28T11:48:46+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Manash Pratim Gohain</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135254522,imgsize-79613.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Process becomes punishment in our system': Ex-SC judge Sanjay Kaul on Umar Khalid, Sharjeel Imam bail pleas]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/process-becomes-punishment-in-our-system-ex-sc-judge-sanjay-kaul-on-umar-khalid-sharjeel-imam-bail-pleas/articleshow/135252397.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135252397.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/process-becomes-punishment-in-our-system-ex-sc-judge-sanjay-kaul-on-umar-khalid-sharjeel-imam-bail-pleas/articleshow/135252397.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/process-becomes-punishment-in-our-system-ex-sc-judge-sanjay-kaul-on-umar-khalid-sharjeel-imam-bail-pleas/articleshow/135252397.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-28T10:33:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid